Begin by rereading the tutorials on the "PLAY" command for Blue Ram. 

The on board "BMUSIC" subroutine IS "PLAY" and the music string is 

identical! Then check the discription of this subroutine in both the 

subroutine manual and the 300 page nutting book to see how to get it 

started. One other thing, the "on board" screen interrupt subroutine 

needs to be running!





*** also check Arcadian Vol5, Issue 4, Page 58. George Moses did more with the music than anyone with maybe Scott Norris that programmed the sounds for most BALLY games.
The PLAY command duplicates how to set up the music generator, only it is done in BASIC instead of ML
Ken***












